id: pm-graph-event-sparse
title: Refresh projections from mutation events with sparse work receipts
description: "Acceptance: after initial admission, one update among 10000 items avoids a complete successful refresh scan; cursor gaps force a disclosed rebuild or refusal; incremental and full projections are equal. Deliver typed SDK and CLI, compact receipts and remedies, seeded state and concurrency tests, non-git public-corpus validation, and npm plus Bun CI release gates."
type: Feature
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-graph#175"
created_at: "2026-10-27T07:16:00.488Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T19:23:18.110Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[42]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T07:16:04.720Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against current CLI and sibling sources: SDK mutation-events owns cursors and history reads; graph snapshot impact compares complete graphs; syncNeo4j in src/index.ts still upserts every input node and relationship. pm-web consumes event pages for resume and history delivery, and pm-rust complete-projection receipts certify reads rather than update a persisted graph. This feature owns only derived projection state, sparse work receipts and sink reconciliation. No upstream or sibling changes planned."
  "2026-10-27T07:24:18.943Z",codex-agent,"Implementation now uses lazy supported SDK package exports, certified complete admission, opaque mutation cursors, SDK point reads, anchor/stream continuity checks, owned checkpoint locking, finite/dense boundary validation, and exact recoverable receipt pages. Explicit rebuild is required after continuity or workspace-schema changes. Cached graph materialization and checkpoint encoding still visit cached rows; receipts separately disclose full source scans and SDK event-page source. Neo4j reconciliation uses a revision CAS inside one write transaction and a separate owned namespace. Seeded model and real-host regressions are being validated."
  "2026-10-27T07:41:59.200Z",codex-agent,"Evidence: seeded model seed 0x261027 passed 500 random sequences through real SDK reads and mutations. The 10000-item non-git case read one updated item with zero complete refresh item scans, evaluated 3 nodes and 2 edges, emitted 814 JSON bytes and equaled both certified full output and an explicit rebuild. Public main corpus at 4b5e7a1: 108 items, 203 nodes, 372 edges, 1138 admission events; caught-up reads/scans/events all zero, 538 JSON bytes, derived_index, 1108 ms admission plus catch-up. Source copy was read-only, authoritative bytes unchanged. Public data exposed omitted legacy dependency metadata; producer JSON normalization and a regression now cover it. Behavioral revert proof: replacing only refreshEventProjection catch-up admission decision with unconditional rebuild makes the sparse regression fail (fullScans 1 versus required 0); implementation restored. All 12 competing-refresher transition boundaries pass, and interrupted-sink retry checks current target revisions."
  "2026-10-27T07:45:20.447Z",codex-agent,"The linked targeted pm test command passed 8/8 tests with no failures or skips; result tracking is disabled by project policy, so the exact command and outcome are recorded here. Additional checks pass for legacy optional dependency fields and custom active/blocked/done/canceled registry roles. Neo4j adapter checks now refuse a dependent delta when a marker, touched node or incident edge is foreign, before graph writes, and preserve driver cleanup. Full npm and Bun release-gate evidence will come from the CI Node matrix; thresholds remain unchanged. No SDK gap or upstream bug required a workaround."
  "2026-10-27T07:48:07.001Z",codex-agent,"Review PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-graph/pull/175. Actual packed admission plus sparse update acceptance passed on all six hosts: npm global, Bun global, npx, bunx, npm local and Bun local. SDK resolution uses only supported package exports, with no executable/symlink lookup. Local typecheck, test typecheck, lint, zero-duplication, build, docstrings and changelog checks pass. Local strict health identifies an existing pm-github extension host-version skew (pinned host 2026.10.20 versus extension host 2026.10.26); the CI clean project installation is the authoritative health gate. Full npm/Bun release-gate run and exact counts will be recorded on the PR after completion. Item remains open for orchestrator verification and is released."
  "2026-10-27T07:51:55.170Z",codex-agent,"Final concurrency review found a driver retry detail: a Neo4j transaction callback may be invoked more than once, so its outcome is reset inside every attempt. The new regression repeats the transaction callback, injects a competing revision, and verifies SINK_CONFLICT rather than a stale success. Targeted Neo4j adapter regression passes. No source behavior or thresholds changed."
  "2026-10-27T08:13:51.896Z",codex-agent,"Re-review round 1 resumed. Rules: storage presence must be independent of decoded payload values, and a rebuild must reset every cursor-derived state field as one generation. Both reported blockers are valid. The package-wide audit covers SDK readers/writers, CLI JSON and TOON, packed npm/Bun hosts and non-git trackers. Main is merged before remediation; no prior completed implementation or validation will be repeated without a new change requiring it."
  "2026-10-27T08:26:33.629Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 class audit: (1) Presence is an out-of-band storage fact, never a decoded JSON value or truthiness decision. readState now returns tagged missing/invalid/present outcomes; only ENOENT permits admission. SDK readEventProjection intentionally retains its nullable read-only contract, while receipt reads refuse invalid payloads. The project manifest and snapshot readers also collapse invalid inputs only on read-only/refusal paths; explicit export output writers do not infer ownership from decoded content. No second writer with this defect was found. (2) Cursor, anchor and subject versions form one event generation. eventGeneration starts all three fresh on rebuild while retaining the previous target revision solely for CAS lineage and old graph rows solely for reconciliation. All fallback and prior-state references, SDK/CLI transports and both graph sinks were checked. No additional non-blocking finding was supplied or found in the class audit."
  "2026-10-27T08:26:35.369Z",codex-agent,"Adversarial evidence: 116 foreign payload cases cover every JSON root type, falsey values, malformed inputs and whitespace/CRLF, with incremental and rebuild attempts, offline and sink targets, plus byte preservation. Empty, workspace-only, item-only and mixed replacement streams rebuild and resume incrementally through real SDK reads; an unchanged pre-fix v1 checkpoint remains readable/exportable. Real non-git CLI JSON/TOON tests passed, including receipt and Neo4j-flag refusal paths. Revert proofs: reverting only readState to classify decoded null as missing makes the storage-presence test fail (admission instead of FOREIGN_STATE); restoring only the old anchor fallback in refreshEventProjection makes the generation test fail with SOURCE_INCOMPLETE on an empty stream. Both processes exited 1, and the fixes were restored. Test and coverage runners now explicitly cap concurrency at two, with thresholds unchanged."
  "2026-10-27T08:54:23.502Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 focused validation passed: pm-linked commands 8/8 existing regressions plus 3/3 new SDK recovery cases; the full new CLI transport case passed separately across JSON and TOON with no git executable. Expanded packed acceptance passed 6/6 hosts (npm/Bun global, npx/bunx, npm/Bun local), each preserving 16 foreign payload variants and rebuilding empty streams in both output formats. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, zero-duplication, build and changelog checks pass. A local full npm gate was started, then intentionally interrupted to honor the original saturated-host instruction to use CI for full-gate evidence; it is not counted as passing. Its test processes have exited. The explicit two-worker limits will apply to both full CI release gates without changing thresholds."
  "2026-10-27T10:11:01.753Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 review: main is already contained and the worktree started clean. Auditing the provenance rule: synthetic reference placeholders must never replace authoritative item nodes, regardless of configured item type or graph labels. Will cover SDK, CLI JSON/TOON, non-git trackers and packed hosts, with behavioral revert proof. No additional non-blocking findings were supplied."
  "2026-10-27T10:14:23.585Z",codex-agent,"Class audit found and fixed a second label/provenance collision in contractionInputFromGraph. A new CLI export equivalence regression also exposed both unconfigured listAllItemMetadata calls: graph export/legacy sync reads and status counts omitted custom type folders. All now use the SDK settings and resolved item type registry. All other package node-role checks use the producer PmItem role; snapshot, blocker, exporter, CLI and Neo4j paths were searched. No schema tightening or stored-format change."
  "2026-10-27T10:16:59.447Z",codex-agent,"Focused round 2 regression passed 3/3: SDK contribution/sink/reference-order and delete/restore model; real no-git refresh/export/contraction JSON/TOON; sparse and legacy Neo4j adapter property writes. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, build, 187/187 documented declarations and zero-percent duplication passed. Packed acceptance is running; full npm/Bun gates will be taken from exact-head CI under two-worker limits."
  "2026-10-27T10:18:19.169Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof (three isolated functions, then restored): (1) restoring label-based placeholder precedence in materialize makes the authoritative contribution SDK/full-graph regression fail, exit 1; (2) removing the PmItem role exclusion in contractionInputFromGraph makes the same regression fail on unexpected unknown nodes, exit 1; (3) removing configured registry/schema arguments from fetchItemsViaSdk and rebuilding dist makes the real no-git CLI export equality regression fail, exit 1. All fixes and built outputs were restored; no existing tests were weakened or deleted."
  "2026-10-27T10:29:27.887Z",codex-agent,"All three linked test commands passed: 8 existing targeted tests, 3 prior recovery tests and 3 current provenance/Neo4j tests (14 reported checks; no failures/skips/cancellations). The final CLI test also independently passed with native graph-export SDK adapter read-back, canonical file exports, JSON/TOON and no git executable. Merged newly advanced main before finishing; incoming tracker histories remain intact. Changelog generation/check, privacy, history-prefix, lint and zero-percent duplication checks passed. The registry reports pm CLI 2026.10.27; the package SDK pin remains unchanged."
  "2026-10-27T10:31:19.078Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance passed 6/6 actual hosts: npm global, Bun global, npx, bunx, npm local and Bun local. Every host preserved authoritative ExternalPmItem fields under a later referencing item, passed JSON/TOON contraction unknown counts, sparse 1-read/0-scan refresh, 16 foreign-payload refusals and both empty-history rebuild formats. Command: node test/event-projection-packed.validation.ts. Round 2 is ready for exact-head CI npm run release:check and bun run release:check (two workers; unchanged thresholds). CI results and run URL will be reported on PR 175; no live Neo4j service was accessed."
  "2026-10-27T11:02:04.092Z",codex-agent,"Bounded CI handoff: after 30 minutes, https://github.com/unbraind/pm-graph/actions/runs/40489166315 at runtime commit 3ddcf79132b1a4c0df549f3d87748d291f323e05 still has all three jobs queued: test (22), test (26), and windows-prepare-lifecycle. Current npm run release:check and bun run release:check counts are unavailable; no current full-gate pass is claimed. Focused linked checks passed 14/14, native exporter adapter equivalence passed, packed hosts passed 6/6, and all three isolated behavioral reverts failed as required. This final evidence-only commit changes tracker receipts, with runtime/tests unchanged. Claim remains released; the item remains unclosed. The queue rule requires stopping after this bounded wait; the orchestrator pipeline can await the pending gates."
  "2026-10-27T11:40:18.987Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 review: worktree started clean and main is already contained. Fixing two classes: ownership predicates must be protected by every lock needed by later destructive writes, and source-preservation fingerprints must include every authoritative input. Auditing sparse and legacy Neo4j sync, tracker/checkpoint CAS paths, generated Cypher, validators and output consumers. Will add competing-session transition tests and independent behavioral revert proofs for locking and schema fingerprints."
  "2026-10-27T12:05:50.340Z",codex-agent,"Class audit: all src Neo4j writes now use lock-protected ownership checks and plain DELETE; sparse, legacy full/incremental sync and generated Cypher share guarded statement producers. Legacy sync is now one transaction. Node/relationship MERGE collisions recheck ownership after acquiring their write lock; native deletion/constraint conflicts map to SINK_CONFLICT and roll back. Tracker checkpoint reads/CAS already occur inside their SDK lease. Consolidated source fingerprints include schema JSON, Markdown and all non-derived regular inputs, with derived-directory exclusions restricted to the tracker root. Four new guard/fingerprint tests and the existing sparse transaction test pass; lint and duplication pass. Real two-session database validation is in progress against an isolated fixture."
  "2026-10-27T13:34:02.402Z",codex-agent,"Fresh read-only public main validation with the corrected complete fingerprint passed: 109 items, 205 nodes, 376 edges, 1160 admission events, one admission scan; catch-up 0 reads/0 scans/0 events, 559-byte JSON, derived_index, 5802 ms measured validation, equal to full and all authoritative source bytes unchanged. SDK createWorkspaceSnapshot supplies the independent authoritative-file oracle in the 500-sequence fingerprint test. Reverting only fingerprint file selection to the former TOON/history/settings filter fails on SDK authoritative schema/fields.json, exit 1; restored. Five focused guard/fingerprint/sparse-transaction tests pass. The isolated real database already passed the focused 18 sparse transition boundaries; the final all-path and packed-host run is in progress."
  "2026-10-27T14:38:10.676Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 class closure: ownership is a transaction invariant, never an unlocked preflight promise. Audited all src Neo4j writes: sparse refresh, legacy incremental/full sync and exported Cypher now use one guarded statement producer and one data transaction; node/relationship write locks precede ownership reads, MERGE rechecks its current target, cleanup deletes only owned relationships then plain nodes, and any foreign/corrupt guard aborts dependents with SINK_CONFLICT. Tracker checkpoint read/modify/publish already holds its SDK lease through publication. No DETACH DELETE remains in src. Source immutability now hashes every authoritative filename and byte across all validators, including schemas; SDK snapshot manifest files are the oracle. Four isolated behavioral reverts exit 1: old syncProjectionDelta loses the real foreign edge at boundary 7; removing the node MERGE predicate admits a late foreign node; removing the edge predicate overwrites a foreign relationship; the old extension filter misses schema/fields.json. Every function/guard was restored. Positive real Neo4j 5.26.27 evidence: 140 query boundaries across sparse, legacy incremental/full and generated Cypher, ordinary/dense nodes, 96 observed server lock waits, five late collision cases; all preserved foreign records/checkpoints. Six actual packed npm/Bun hosts on SDK 2026.10.20 pass 48 JSON/TOON incremental/rebuild refusals and sparse retries. All four linked commands pass 18 reported tests, no skips/failures. Main advanced during validation; merged fc2410b in 2e296a7, installed its SDK/toolchain 2026.10.23, and the packed validator now derives that pin for CI. Final focused checks against the merged pin follow; full npm/Bun gates remain CI evidence."
  "2026-10-27T14:46:16.656Z",codex-agent,"Final local round-3 evidence after the main merge and SDK 2026.10.23 install: guard/fingerprint tests pass 4/4; Cypher export/command and legacy incremental/full/empty sync tests pass 4/4. Their initial schema-context run rerouted fixture initialization and failed before product execution; the supported linked-test snapshot workspace plus none PM context now passes without changing assertions. Standard pinned pm-github installer cleared clone-local host-version skew; strict pm health now exits 0 with zero warnings and valid append-only history. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, 0-percent duplication, build and 193/193 docstrings pass. The read-only non-git public copy at 42e20bb revalidated with SDK 2026.10.23: 109 items, 205 nodes, 376 edges, 1160 admission events, one admission scan; caught-up reads/scans/events all zero, 559 JSON bytes, derived_index, equal to full, all authoritative bytes including schemas unchanged, 4617 ms. Prior four linked commands passed 18 reported tests; merged-pin focused commands pass another 8 reported checks. Real-server interleavings/collisions and six SDK-2026.10.20 packed compatibility hosts remain the measured evidence in the previous comment; CI uses the merged pin for the full npm/Bun gates and live packed fixture. Releasing the claim without closing; ready PR 175 will receive the exact-head CI run link and counts or the required bounded pending receipt."
  "2026-10-27T15:05:32.945Z",codex-agent,"During the bounded CI wait, checked dense-node lock semantics against the official Neo4j concurrent-access manual. Dense relationship creation can use node-delete prevention locks independently of NODE property-write locks. Extended the native fixture with a pure foreign-edge writer in addition to the NODE-write probe: default CI now exercises both, and a focused edges-only run validates the additional 140 boundaries against the merged SDK. Query-complete peer transactions observed Closing are rolled back from the projection side without being misreported as confirmed NODE lock waits. This strengthens class coverage; production queries and schemas are unchanged. Reclaimed for this test-only completion before the final handoff."
  "2026-10-27T15:23:08.233Z",codex-agent,"Additional class evidence completed: all 140 pure foreign-edge boundaries pass on SDK 2026.10.23 across sparse, legacy incremental/full and generated Cypher on ordinary/dense nodes. Observed 80 explicit Blocked states and 16 separately reported Closing-state rollbacks; all actual foreign edges and checkpoints survive. Combined local native evidence is 280 boundaries (140 NODE probes plus 140 pure-edge writers), five late collisions and 48 packed-host refusals. Pure-edge behavioral revert: restoring only the old syncProjectionDelta loses the real foreign edge at boundary 7, exit 1, without a peer property write. This is the fifth negative proof run across four distinct mutants; every function is restored and src/dist are byte-identical to f6d81a6. Updated fixture types/lint pass and duplication remains zero. The required 30-minute runtime CI wait elapsed: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-graph/actions/runs/40524807745 for f6d81a6 has all three jobs queued, no active steps, no npm/Bun full-gate counts. New test-only head checks will remain explicitly pending; no pass is inferred. Greptile reports an expired trial rather than a review; there are no inline findings, and no review approval is claimed. Releasing the claim again, leaving the item in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-27T15:24:53.229Z",codex-agent,"Exact test-head handoff: 95281c50d43579958623f6421c7fafd14b8baca4 contains the 280-boundary native fixture; authored runtime/generated output are unchanged from f6d81a6. CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-graph/actions/runs/40530474274 is queued, so current npm/Bun release-gate counts are unavailable. The prior runtime CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-graph/actions/runs/40524807745 remained queued with all three jobs unstarted after the required 30-minute bounded wait. No full-gate success or external-review approval is claimed. Claim is released, item remains in progress; subsequent receipt-only commit changes no runtime or tests. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-graph/pull/175 is ready for review, not merged or released."
  "2026-10-27T16:22:55.026Z",codex-agent,"Round 4 class: durable post-action recovery must reconcile the sink authority before planning newer source work. Current retry recomputes a new payload from the stale checkpoint, so a committed sink revision becomes unreachable after source updates. Plan: persist owned recovery intent before sink action; commit native source-history coordinates with the sink revision in the same transaction; inspect/reconcile the marker before source guards, adopt a verified committed intent, then continue mutation catch-up. Explicit rebuild reads the current marker, certifies the current source and reconciles the complete owned projection under ownership guards. Audit all checkpoint/sink/receipt paths, retain prior-schema compatibility and foreign-data refusals, add seeded crash/source-update model tests plus real Neo4j and packed JSON/TOON checks. Main is current; no merge required."
  "2026-10-27T16:49:12.351Z",codex-agent,"Round-4 implementation and evidence: recovery intent is atomically stored before action using the unchanged v1 checkpoint validator. Neo4j commits the native SDK cursor/anchor with revision in the same transaction, inspects that authority before new planning, adopts a source-verified committed intent, and continues sparse events. Missing cached contributions for a source-known marker disclose a certified rebuild; source-unknown markers refuse ordinary refresh. Explicit rebuild CAS binds the current observed target revision, resets only owned edges, preserves foreign edges on retained nodes, and prunes only stale owned nodes under ownership locks. Source status/history/normalization remain SDK-owned. Audited legacy sync (no separate post-transaction checkpoint), offline atomic checkpoint/receipt, custom CAS compatibility, CLI JSON/TOON, and packed hosts. New 500-sequence model passes across three post-action crash phases, 0-3 source updates, admission/existing checkpoints, both modes, older-input replay, native fields, relationships and custom roles; all values come from SDK read-back. Real Neo4j passes all 24 phase/update/mode combinations and matches a full reference written through the same SDK sink, retaining a foreign relationship. Isolated changed-function revert reproduces SINK_CONFLICT after source advances; restored copy passes. Types/lint/zero duplication/build/202 docstrings pass. Packed six-host recovery checks are running."
  "2026-10-27T17:28:52.116Z",codex-agent,"The previous-head CI run 40531036817 failed its exact Cypher-row consumer test (Node 26: 431/432 passed). SDK budget receipts explicitly marked strings_compacted; the test incorrectly executed shortened row fields. The consumer now recovers the identical cursor window with the SDK amount and unbounded-cost controls, then retains the original exact row/order equality and all cursor/budget assertions. Focused packaged-host Cypher recovery passes (1/1). Documentation explains exact-field recovery; no SQL guard or production row format was weakened. The separate compatibility/ownership regression files pass 6/6, including foreign JSON, prior-producer v1, non-git JSON/TOON and all guarded writes. Read-only marker inspection now has an additional malformed-row/legacy-row corpus (1/1)."
  "2026-10-27T17:30:27.339Z",codex-agent,"Whole-class audit: inspected every source checkpoint publication, revision comparison, Neo4j transaction, SDK sink and CLI adapter. Both refresh surfaces now use the same durable-intent/revision recovery implementation and the public built-in sink factory; legacy sync and generated Cypher retain the shared ownership guards and have no separate persisted post-action checkpoint. JSON/TOON and six installation hosts exercise the same adapter. Recovery revalidates even an unchanged target after inspection; event version lookups use Map for arbitrary native identities. Revalidated the read-only public main corpus: 109 items, 205 nodes, 376 edges, 1160 admission events; admission 1 scan, caught-up 0 scans/0 reads/0 events, 559-byte JSON, 17775 ms on the shared host, derived_index, full equality, every authoritative filename and byte unchanged including schema JSON."
  "2026-10-27T17:32:46.376Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof (disposable copy, fixed worktree untouched): node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='legacy CAS sink recovers' test/event-projection-post-action.test.ts. Reverting only refreshEventProjection to the prior implementation yields 0/1 passing and SINK_CONFLICT after sink commit, lost checkpoint and later source mutation, exit 1. Restoring that function yields 1/1 passing, covering both ordinary sparse retry and explicit rebuild. All earlier foreign-data, empty-history, type-provenance, transaction-lock and schema-fingerprint regressions are retained."
  "2026-10-27T17:33:18.461Z",codex-agent,"Final focused checks: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/event-projection-neo4j.test.ts passes 1/1, including explicit full rebuild of owned data; native marker corpus passes 1/1. npm run build:test, npm run typecheck, npm run lint, npm run duplication and npm run docstring pass: zero duplication, all 202 documented declarations. Full release suites remain CI-only at unchanged thresholds and two workers. The real packed acceptance now captures and verifies one 52-file archive with SHA-256 2bad3b24720e612f95a2f59dfb62b8e59fdc7d9db11edfed80c4390b1af50420; all six consumers share these exact bytes. Final host results are still in progress."
  "2026-10-27T17:41:50.313Z",codex-agent,"Added empty-native-history post-action recovery coverage using the existing scratch-only history reset helper (SDK init emits a workspace event). Both ordinary sparse recovery and explicit rebuild pass after a committed empty generation and later item creation. An opaque observed target revision refuses ordinary catch-up, while explicit rebuild binds that current revision and converges. Focused empty-history/opaque-revision regression passes 1/1 across both modes. Full 500-sequence linked rerun remains in progress on the shared host."
  "2026-10-27T17:48:53.765Z",codex-agent,"Final archive npm-global acceptance passes: eight actual Neo4j foreign-record refusals, checkpoint preservation, sparse retry with two reads, and four native post-action recoveries (JSON/TOON by incremental/rebuild). Remaining hosts are running. Expanded the native before/after-query matrix and late-node collision corpus to include explicit projection rebuild, because its new owned-edge reset/stale-node pruning is another write path of the same ownership class. The focused rebuild variant runs both node-probe and pure-edge writers on ordinary/dense nodes; default CI now includes it alongside every existing path."
  "2026-10-27T17:58:00.959Z",codex-agent,"Final linked 500-sequence rerun reached its explicit 1800-second shared-host timeout: critical legacy-CAS regression passed, 200 sequences were reported, then the runner terminated its child with SIGTERM (exit 5; timeout, no assertion failure reported). This is incomplete evidence, not a pass. Earlier complete runs passed all 500 sequences (direct run 3/3 and linked run 4/4 before the additional boundary cases). Current focused boundary tests pass separately, including malformed/reordered/competing markers and empty history/opaque revisions. No further full local rerun will burden the saturated host; exact-head CI will run the entire property suite at unchanged thresholds/two workers. Packed npm-global current-artifact checks pass; other hosts remain active."
  "2026-10-27T18:25:35.419Z",codex-agent,"Clarified the durable-recovery contract: adopting a verified earlier sink commit can publish its checkpoint before a later source/ownership refusal. Successful committed history is retained, never rolled back to erase that later refusal. The strengthened competing-marker regression passes 1/1 and asserts the adopted checkpoint revision remains in the sink audit after the later SINK_CONFLICT. Source/generated changes here are documentation only; executable JavaScript remains byte-identical to bfe8899. Verified the captured 52-file archive digest and all nine runtime/declaration/map files against bfe8899 before this declaration-comment clarification; preserved the private artifact without tracking binaries. Current archive has passed npm global, Bun global, npx and bunx: 32 real foreign-data refusals and 16 crash recoveries. Project-local hosts continue."
  "2026-10-27T18:35:37.187Z",codex-agent,"Final six-host packed acceptance passes on SDK 2026.10.23: npm-global, bun-global, npx, bunx, npm-local and bun-local, all using the same 52-file archive (SHA-256 2bad3b24720e612f95a2f59dfb62b8e59fdc7d9db11edfed80c4390b1af50420). Total: 48 actual Neo4j foreign-record refusals with retained checkpoints, plus 24 native post-action recoveries across JSON/TOON and normal/rebuild; source values read through each real SDK host equal target values and foreign edges survive. Sparse retries use two point reads and zero full scans. Original archive digest remains unchanged after every host; private bytes were preserved, with no tracked binary. Its nine runtime/declaration/map files matched bfe8899; subsequent declaration-comment/test-report changes do not alter executable JS. The isolated packed fixture stopped cleanly. Running the additional explicit-rebuild interleaving matrix through linked test 8 (none/snapshot context, operator fixture path passed only at execution)."
  "2026-10-27T18:41:11.626Z",codex-agent,"Final linked test 8 passes: explicit projection rebuild, both node-probe and pure foreign-edge writers on ordinary/dense nodes, all 96 query boundaries. Observed 60 actual Blocked transitions and eight separately reported Closing-state rollbacks. Every real foreign edge survives, every refusal is typed SINK_CONFLICT, and checkpoint bytes remain unchanged. This adds 96 measured boundaries to the retained 280 from the earlier ownership audit. The isolated server stopped cleanly. Final current checks pass build/test types, source types, lint, zero duplication and 202 documented declarations. All six packed hosts pass 48 ownership refusals plus 24 crash recoveries; real post-action matrix passes 24 combinations; the changed-function revert fails as required and restoration passes. Two prior 500-sequence runs pass; the last resource-limited rerun timed out at 30 minutes after 200 reported sequences and is explicitly incomplete. No local full release suite was run on the saturated host. Final exact-head npm/Bun release evidence will be reported at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-graph/pull/175/checks and in the linked PR body/final handoff; no pending check is a pass. Completing tracker writes before final CI verification, leaving this item in progress and releasing only this claim."
